What is the bug in this loop?

```c
int i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
    printf("%d\n", i);
}
```

It's an **infinite loop**: `i` is never incremented, so `i < 10` stays true and it prints `0` forever.

Fix:

```c
int i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
    printf("%d\n", i);
    i++;
}
```

